WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:06.260
Hey David, can you delineate the factions
that exist on the left right now?

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:08.200
So I'll try to do this.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:14.450
No, I don't think that anyone will agree about
the different factions on the left that exist.

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:15.450
Right.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.160
Everybody would delineate it a little bit
differently, but I'll give you my take on

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:22.320
it and you know with the caveat that there
is overlap between some of these groups and

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.590
there is some fluidity between some of these
groups.

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:32.750
So you have what is called third way politics,
which exists in both the democratic and the

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:34.570
Republican party.

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:42.579
But it is in a sense it is, it is sort of
a center left centrism you could argue that

00:00:42.579 --> 00:00:46.989
like bill Clinton, uh, personified this to
some degree.

00:00:46.989 --> 00:00:52.490
There is third way we can call it third way
centrism which is a faction on the left.

00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:55.850
It's a pretty establishment faction of the
left.

00:00:55.850 --> 00:01:00.219
Some of you might call these establishment
shills although that's a pejorative term.

00:01:00.219 --> 00:01:02.440
So that's kind of one faction of the left.

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:06.580
And I, and I know that that one can be characterized
in a, in a few different ways.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:11.960
There is what I call modern progressivism
and another way to sort of call that would

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.680
be true social democracy.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:15.680
Okay.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:18.490
So these are definitely capitalists.

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:26.220
These are people who don't want to destroy
the system that we have are buying large incremental

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:31.030
lists, who have seen the successes of social
democracy in other countries and they want

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:36.400
to move in that direction on the basis that
there are specific policy ideas, which if

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:42.220
we elect the right people, the system that
currently exists can be tweaked and we can

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:47.310
go in a direction that would be often more
like the Scandinavian economic and social

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:48.310
model.

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:52.560
That's what I call modern progressivism, which
takes into account, um, things like Medicare

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.790
for all or some other way of getting to universal
coverage.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:02:01.440
We're talking about, um, in many cases, housing
subsidies, we're talking about maybe like

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:08.759
Bernie's plan to make tuition of at state
and local state a, um, uh, schools, uh, tuition

00:02:08.759 --> 00:02:09.759
free.

00:02:09.759 --> 00:02:14.270
Uh, you're talking about paid maternity leave,
you're talking about a democratization of

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:16.840
the workplace to different degrees.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.380
Still capitalism.

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:21.510
Modern progressivism is sort of like true
social democracy.

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:25.840
You then have actual democratic socialism.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:26.840
Okay.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:29.410
Which is a smaller subsection.

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:35.450
Um, in the immediate, a lot of their goals
are very similar to those of the modern Progressive's

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:38.200
in that the next steps are very similar.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:43.231
They may want to totally socialize the means
of ownership of the means of production, but

00:02:43.231 --> 00:02:48.170
for the most part the democratic socialists
will often agree that the next step for their

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:52.890
cause is the same one as for social Democrats,
which is we need to make sure that we are

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:59.590
supporting um, uh, workers rights and labor
when it comes to health care.

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:04.940
Modern Progressive's and democratic socialists
for the most part want something like Medicare

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:06.019
for all.

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:08.769
Although they may disagree about the way to
implement it.

00:03:08.769 --> 00:03:11.930
And this is actually going to relate to our
next audience question, which is about, is

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:15.860
the debate between social Democrats and democratic
socialists one worth having right now.

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:16.879
But I'll get to that later.

00:03:16.879 --> 00:03:19.769
So that's your democratic socialists.

00:03:19.769 --> 00:03:22.040
And this is a term that's often misapplied.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:25.711
You will often have people who call themselves
democratic socialists who really aren't, they're

00:03:25.711 --> 00:03:27.010
just modern progressives.

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:28.069
They're social Democrats.

00:03:28.069 --> 00:03:30.370
They don't want to socialize the means of
production.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:33.970
They don't want the government as involved
as an actual Democrat democratic socialists

00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:36.209
might want.

00:03:36.209 --> 00:03:43.140
Then we get to, and this is where it starts
to get a little tough, we get to what I believe

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:46.910
are some of the fringe groups and I want to
be careful about what term to use.

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:50.130
I'm not trying to be pejorative, although
I think that these groups often have a lot

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:51.250
of bad ideas.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:56.670
You have a sort of, you've got what sometimes
is called the Leninist left.

00:03:56.670 --> 00:04:01.270
You have what sometimes are called tankinis
and I know that that's a pejorative term.

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:03.230
I'm trying to find a non pejorative.

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:10.470
There is sometimes overlap with a sort of
more anarchistic movement within the left.

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:16.979
These are relatively fringe and you will find
that they have overlap with some of these

00:04:16.979 --> 00:04:20.079
other groups on foreign policy.

00:04:20.079 --> 00:04:26.199
You will sometimes see overlap between the
Leninist left tanky types, uh, and democratic

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:29.089
socialists, although maybe for different reasons.

00:04:29.089 --> 00:04:35.199
For example, you might have isolationists
and non interventionists who are actually

00:04:35.199 --> 00:04:39.770
different politically that sometimes we'll
agree on what the policy should be.

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:43.349
In a particular foreign policy situation.

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:50.520
You will have Leninist left tanky types and
social Democrats who might agree on how should

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:53.919
education and healthcare be dealt with for
example.

00:04:53.919 --> 00:05:00.729
Um, but there are definitely some framing
differences where the Lennon is left tanky

00:05:00.729 --> 00:05:04.939
side and I, if somebody has a better now I
want a non pejorative term for that group,

00:05:04.939 --> 00:05:06.949
please tell me what one would be.

00:05:06.949 --> 00:05:14.499
Um, if there are times where when you get
into conversations of very basic things like

00:05:14.499 --> 00:05:20.389
the concept of a nation state, um, should
militaries exist where you will get to like

00:05:20.389 --> 00:05:23.009
some pretty stark differences.

00:05:23.009 --> 00:05:29.889
There are, there is also a strong actual socialist
communist component, um, within the Leninist

00:05:29.889 --> 00:05:33.719
left as the name probably suggests to you.

00:05:33.719 --> 00:05:37.520
Um, that is how I see the divisions on the
left right now.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:41.509
And I think for the most part think that it's
great to have these different factions.

00:05:41.509 --> 00:05:48.909
You know, the Republican party ha prior to
Trump did not suffer greatly because of the

00:05:48.909 --> 00:05:57.669
three way split between the tea party types,
religious conservatives and pro-business Republicans.

00:05:57.669 --> 00:06:02.800
They had all three, they won thousands of
seats at the local level and up.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:05.179
Um, and it did not do damage to them.

00:06:05.179 --> 00:06:10.889
And I see no problem with having all of these
different groups included in the context of,

00:06:10.889 --> 00:06:14.330
uh, the left when it starts to become toxic.

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:18.639
And we've talked about when it does, I think
it does start to do damage to the movement.

00:06:18.639 --> 00:06:23.319
If you disagree with how I see the modern
left being divided up, let me know and please

00:06:23.319 --> 00:06:25.589
do let me know some other way to refer to
the Lennon.

00:06:25.589 --> 00:06:26.969
It's left tanky types.

00:06:26.969 --> 00:06:28.919
Uh, I don't want it to be pejorative.

00:06:28.919 --> 00:06:32.749
It also can't be gushing right, because I
do think that there are major problems with

00:06:32.749 --> 00:06:33.199
that, with that movement

